Copy
Edit
NDVI = (B8 - B4) / (B8 + B4)
B4 (Red): Sentinel-2 Band 4

B8 (NIR): Sentinel-2 Band 8

NDVI Interpretation
NDVI Value	Interpretation
-1.0 to 0.0	Water
~0.0 to 0.1	Barren rock, sand, or snow
0.2 to 0.4	Shrubs and grasslands
0.4 and higher	Temperate/tropical forests

By isolating NDVI values greater than 0.2, we can identify areas with likely vegetation.

Elevation & Vegetation
Overlaying NDVI data with a Digital Elevation Model (DEM) allows us to:

Define upper and lower vegetation boundaries.

Create interpolated surfaces of vegetation extent by elevation.

Track how these vegetation elevation contours shift over time.

This enables predictions of whether vegetation will retreat or advance to certain altitudes in the future — vital for anticipating ecosystem shifts.

Outcomes
Identify upper elevation limits where vegetation meets rock/snow.

Identify lower elevation limits where vegetation meets water.

Ability to track temporal changes in vegetation boundaries.

Ability to forecast future vegetation zones under continued warming.

Summary
This project combines NDVI, elevation data, and time-series analysis to monitor and predict how vegetation adapts to climate change in a rapidly evolving alpine landscape.

